[GitHub](https://github.com/AJBogo9/bayesian-fatality-analysis){.btn .btn-outline-secondary .btn-sm}

A study of fatality-rate patterns across aircraft manufacturers, fitting hierarchical and non-hierarchical Bayesian models in R with `brms` (Stan backend) to 1,766 aviation crashes spanning 40 manufacturers from 1976 to 2024.

## The question

Are some manufacturers genuinely safer than others, or do apparent differences vanish once you account for how few crashes each manufacturer contributes? A naive per-manufacturer rate is noisy; complete pooling hides real variation. Hierarchical partial pooling sits between the two.

## What the models showed

The hierarchical partial-pooling model outperformed complete pooling by **1,944 ELPD points**, confirming significant manufacturer-level variation in fatality rates that persists despite industry standardisation. The temporal trend, by contrast, was minimal.
